This file records every third-party component this program links, bundles or
requires, with its licence and the reason it is here. GPL-2.0 is the project's
licence and every entry below is compatible with it.


LINKED LIBRARIES
================

cairo                            LGPL-2.1 or MPL-1.1 (dual)
    All drawing. This program has no toolkit: the login screen is composed by
    hand into an ARGB32 image surface and blitted once to an Xlib surface.
    Also reads PNG natively, which is why only JPEG needs a separate decoder.

FreeType                         FTL (BSD-style) or GPL-2.0 (dual)
    Font rasterisation, through cairo's FreeType backend. Used directly rather
    than through fontconfig so the two bundled faces can be loaded by path --
    a login screen draws before any user profile exists and must not depend on
    a working fontconfig cache.

libX11 (Xlib)                    MIT
    The window, the event loop, the keyboard grab and the input method. No
    toolkit sits between this program and the X server.

libXrandr                        MIT
    Finding the primary output, so that on a two-monitor machine the login
    panel is centred on one screen rather than across the bezel.

libjpeg-turbo                    IJG (BSD-style)
    JPEG background images, and nothing else. Cairo reads PNG and does not
    read JPEG; that is the entire reason this dependency exists. The decoder
    runs as root before anybody has authenticated, so its default error
    handler -- which calls exit() -- is replaced, and both the file size and
    the pixel dimensions are capped before it is handed anything.

Linux-PAM (libpam)               BSD-3-Clause or GPL-2.0 (dual)
    Authentication. Every decision about whether a password is correct, an
    account is valid or a session may be opened belongs to PAM and to
    /etc/pam.d/xlogin, not to this program.


BUNDLED FONTS
=============

Installed to <prefix>/share/xlogin/fonts/ and loaded by path. Their licence
texts are installed alongside them.

Michroma                         SIL Open Font License 1.1
    Copyright the Michroma Project Authors.
    The title face. Licence text: fonts/Michroma-OFL.txt

Roboto                           Apache License 2.0
    Copyright the Roboto Project Authors.
    Everything else on the screen. Licence text: fonts/Roboto-LICENSE.txt

Both are bundled rather than resolved through fontconfig, for the reason given
under FreeType above. Neither is modified.


RUNTIME PROGRAMS
================

Not linked, and each one located by probing an absolute path -- never through
$PATH, and never through a shell.

shutdown(8)                      part of sysvinit-core (GPL-2.0)
    The Shutdown and Restart entries in the Options menu. Found by probing
    /usr/sbin/shutdown, /sbin/shutdown, /usr/bin/shutdown and /bin/shutdown
    with access(X_OK) at the moment it is needed, because /sbin is a symlink
    to /usr/sbin on some systems and a real directory on others.

/bin/sh                          whatever the system provides
    Used once, to run the user's ~/.xinitrc -- which is a shell script, so
    there is no way to run it that is not a shell. It happens after the
    privilege drop, as the target user, never as root.

No other external program is run. In particular this program does not use
chvt(1) (it issues the VT_ACTIVATE ioctl itself), pkill(1) (it walks /proc
itself) or xsetroot(1) (its own window covers the screen).
